team_fallback:
  current: single lead agent (controller) dispatching fresh subagents per task and
    review, via superpowers:subagent-driven-development
  reason: bounded, well-specified feature with a pre-approved design and a fully
    regenerated implementation plan; task-scoped review plus a final whole-branch
    review gave independent-challenge coverage without needing a persistent team
  lost_challenge: >-
    a truly independent second implementer team; mitigated by dispatching each task
    to a fresh subagent with no memory of prior tasks' choices, a separate reviewer
    subagent for every task (never the implementer grading its own work), a
    most-capable-model final whole-branch review that re-executed code rather than
    trusting the diff, and two decisions (kustomize-render approach, naming
    convention) explicitly escalated to the human rather than resolved unilaterally
